00:11:57.820 --> 00:11:58.420
Karen enters.

252
00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:00.400
She's a little curious, like, what are you doing?

253
00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:02.340
And he's like, it's too hard to explain.

254
00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:07.920
And we see a talking head where Jim says that he stole some of Dwight's stationery before he left.

255
00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:13.360
And he occasionally sends Dwight a fax from Dwight's future self.

256
00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:14.580
It's so good.

257
00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:15.880
It's so perfect.

258
00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:17.120
It's so perfect.

259
00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:20.940
And that morning he said, don't drink the coffee.

260
00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:22.520
Might be poisoned, right?

261
00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:23.400
Something to that effect.

262
00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:24.720
So Dwight's like, oh, my God.

263
00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:27.460
And he sees Stanley about to take a sip of coffee.

264
00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:29.700
And he, you know, practically tackles him to the ground.

265
00:12:29.840 --> 00:12:30.960
He's like, you'll thank me later.

266
00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:37.320
So Dwight thinks he is getting faxes from his future self.

267
00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:39.080
This is classic Jim.

268
00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:40.420
It's so good.

269
00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:46.160
The first thing I thought after I watched this cold open was, did Mike Schur write this episode?

270
00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:47.080
He did.

271
00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:48.260
Because that's Mike Schur.

272
00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:51.540
This is 100% from the brain of Mike Schur.

273
00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:55.580
He did such a good job of writing these Jim Dwight pranks.

274
00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:56.860
Oh, he's so smart, Jenna.

275
00:12:57.100 --> 00:12:57.840
He's so smart.

276
00:12:58.000 --> 00:12:58.260
I know.

277
00:12:58.600 --> 00:12:59.000
He's smarty.

278
00:12:59.000 --> 00:12:59.500
Yeah.

279
00:12:59.800 --> 00:12:59.960
All right.

280
00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:03.440
So then we move into the episode and Michael is at his desk.

281
00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:04.580
Jan enters.

282
00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:06.160
Oh, Michael.

283
00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:08.320
Again, like three hellos.

284
00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:11.020
Just call me Levinson in the morning.

285
00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:13.160
In the morning, Levinson's.

286
00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:16.620
And, you know, Jan has news to deliver.

287
00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:21.240
But first she has to sit through this barrage of awkward hellos from Michael.

288
00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:26.040
And she finally tells him, Dunder Mifflin Scranton is closing.

289
00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:28.680
You are a severance package person.

290
00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:28.960
Yeah.

291
00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:30.340
You're not going to make it.

292
00:13:30.560 --> 00:13:31.140
Michael starts crying.

293
00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:33.780
And then he starts like moaning.

294
00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:34.740
Like how awkward.

295
00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:37.840
Jenna, can you imagine like in this moment?

296
00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:38.940
No.

297
00:13:39.100 --> 00:13:40.400
And of course, it's so loud.

298
00:13:40.580 --> 00:13:46.240
Everyone from outside the office can see and hear that something is going down in his office.

299
00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:47.540
Everyone's very curious.

300
00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:51.900
Yes, because he's like, like he's moaning.

301
00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:55.960
Kevin comes over to Pam's desk, wants to know what's going on.

302
00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:58.080
We had a fan question.

303
00:13:58.740 --> 00:13:59.340
Okay.

304
00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:01.520
I'm going to let this fan question go.

305
00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:05.640
And then I have a card that just says, what?

306
00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:08.880
What is it what Hadley Horton is wondering?

307
00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:11.080
Why is Pam's hair different?

308
00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:12.620
What's up with the low pony?

309
00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:16.940
Oh, that's a separate card called low pony question mark.

310
00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:17.720
Okay.

311
00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:19.360
Where should we start?

312
00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.960
Should we start with what or low pony?

313
00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:24.780
Let's start with what and then go into low pony.

314
00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:25.560
Great.

315
00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:31.380
Pam calls Kevin Kev and then Buddy and they fist bump.

316
00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:32.480
What is happening?

317
00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:34.160
What is happening?

318
00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:37.360
The fist bump was a reluctant fist bump though, Ange.

319
00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:39.520
I know, but Kev, Buddy, fist bump.

320
00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:40.180
She's being condescending.

321
00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:42.180
She's being totally condescending.

322
00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:43.600
She's trying to put him off.

323
00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:47.840
She's like, Kev, Buddy, fist bump, leave my desk.

324
00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:50.500
I mean, she's trying to get through it.

325
00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:51.820
That's my interpretation.

326
00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:55.740
My interpretation was that he's like a little kid.

327
00:14:56.140 --> 00:14:56.500
Yeah.

328
00:14:56.840 --> 00:14:57.140
Yeah.

329
00:14:57.340 --> 00:14:58.320
So she's like, okay, Kev.

330
00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:00.520
She's patronizing him for sure.

331
00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:07.680
But you just don't often hear Pam sort of become that casual with Kevin or, you know,

332
00:15:07.780 --> 00:15:10.960
I feel like she saves that part of herself for Jim and everyone else.

333
00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:14.180
She's sort of just aloof to a little bit.

334
00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:17.800
So it just kind of was startling to me that and your low ponytail.

335
00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:19.080
I mean, what the heck?

336
00:15:19.820 --> 00:15:21.520
Here's the deal with the low pony.

337
00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:23.680
I think it was a swing and a miss.

338
00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:27.620
I wasn't crazy about it when I saw it.

339
00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:30.580
We were trying to change things up.

340
00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:36.620
You might notice as well, Pam has got a little bit of like a pinkier, sparklier eyeshadow on

341
00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:38.780
in this episode as well and a little lip gloss.

342
00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:39.700
There's so much pink.

343
00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:42.800
She has pink eyeshadow, pink lipstick, pink sweater.

344
00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:48.020
But then the low pony with the clip, not even a ponytail holder.

345
00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:49.280
I can't wait.

346
00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:49.540
Wait.

347
00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:50.440
I sounded so Southern.

348
00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:51.660
It's very hard for me.

349
00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:52.460
Holder.

350
00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:56.240
Anyway, it's a clip holding your hair, not even a ponytail holder.

351
00:15:56.780 --> 00:15:57.340
Yeah.

352
00:15:57.620 --> 00:15:59.460
Well, the clip is humongous.

353
00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:00.880
Here's the thing.

354
00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:09.640
The conversation in hair and makeup was that Pam would be experimenting a little bit because

355
00:16:09.640 --> 00:16:11.600
she's going to her art classes.

356
00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:13.340
She's living on her own.

357
00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:21.340
We needed to see some physical representation of the fact that she's attempting even in small

358
00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:24.720
ways to break out of her shell right now, to break out of her routines.

359
00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:27.140
So there you go.

360
00:16:27.140 --> 00:16:28.900
We offer the low pony.

361
00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:35.760
I'm going to say I think you never see it again because it wasn't great.

362
00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:37.880
Can we just say it wasn't great?

363
00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:39.280
It's a clip low pony.

364
00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:40.400
Yeah.

365
00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:41.320
A clip low pony.

366
00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:44.040
Now, I kind of wish they'd really gone for it.

367
00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:45.760
Next week, you would have had a banana clip.

368
00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:46.800
Remember those things?

369
00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:47.300
Oh, God.

370
00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:48.780
They gave you like a mohawk.

371
00:16:49.620 --> 00:16:50.060
Yeah.

372
00:16:50.380 --> 00:16:50.640
Yeah.

373
00:16:51.080 --> 00:16:51.660
All right.

374
00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:53.800
Well, it was a moment in time.

375
00:16:54.020 --> 00:16:55.480
It was something we tried.

376
00:16:56.440 --> 00:16:59.720
Unfortunately, it's there for us all to see again and again.

377
00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:00.200
Okay.

378
00:17:00.340 --> 00:17:02.000
Don't say unfortunately to me.

379
00:17:02.140 --> 00:17:04.400
Do you see how many low ponies my character has?

380
00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:06.240
Like all the crazy hair dudes I have?

381
00:17:06.240 --> 00:17:08.040
Listen, I don't have a problem with a low pony.

382
00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:10.180
I don't have a problem with a low pony in general.

383
00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:15.400
I'm just saying this particular low pony was because of the giant clip.

384
00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:16.800
It was odd.

385
00:17:17.860 --> 00:17:19.680
We're back in Michael's office.

386
00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:23.200
And Jenna, I don't know if you've ever had to fire someone.

387
00:17:23.260 --> 00:17:24.260
I have.

388
00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:26.160
Or if you've ever been fired.

389
00:17:26.380 --> 00:17:29.220
But I couldn't imagine getting the news Michael got.

390
00:17:29.420 --> 00:17:36.620
And Jan's like, well, you know, they believe that Josh Porter is going to have a big role in the future of the company.

391
00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:38.980
And Michael goes, what kind of role?

392
00:17:39.140 --> 00:17:40.760
The king of the stupid universe.

393
00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:42.180
Yeah.

394
00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:44.020
Could you imagine?

395
00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:49.200
Like firing someone, basically, who's having this kind of a spiral?

396
00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:49.800
I mean.

397
00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:56.040
Could you imagine firing someone or being fired and then having their wind up mechanical teeth?

398
00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:57.000
Was that in the script?

399
00:17:57.280 --> 00:17:58.240
It was an accident.

400
00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:09.060
And by the way, this points to what amazing actors Steve and Melora are because they just stayed in the moment and reacted to it as if that was meant to happen.

401
00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:10.540
It was not meant to happen.

402
00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:19.900
And could it be more brilliant that you're firing this guy who's so incompetent on so many levels and his clacky teeth go off?

403
00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:21.740
Yes.

404
00:18:22.480 --> 00:18:23.080
Amazing.

405
00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:24.020
All right.

406
00:18:24.380 --> 00:18:25.640
I'm going to move us along.

407
00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:31.520
Michael has a talking head where he says, let's see Josh find another Stanley, Phyllis, or Kevin.

408
00:18:31.740 --> 00:18:32.740
Show me that farm.

409
00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:34.340
Show me that farm.

410
00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:41.000
And during that talking head, we kind of, we see Creed eating his mung beans at his desk.

411
00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:43.340
We see Phyllis knitting.

412
00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:45.580
And we had a fan question from Stephanie Miller.

413
00:18:45.880 --> 00:18:49.620
In this episode, when we see Phyllis knitting, can she knit in real life?

414
00:18:49.740 --> 00:18:52.320
Did she knit that whole scarf her character is working on?

415
00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:55.280
You guys, she is 100% fake knitting.

416
00:18:55.560 --> 00:18:56.600
Phyllis cannot knit.

417
00:18:57.220 --> 00:18:58.400
Didn't she do so good?

418
00:18:58.420 --> 00:19:00.360
They had a basket full of knitting stuff.

419
00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:01.700
They'd made it part of her character.

420
00:19:01.880 --> 00:19:05.180
It's set next to her desk all nine seasons.

421
00:19:05.780 --> 00:19:06.920
And it just sat there.

422
00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:08.740
And sometimes if she had to do background stuff.

423
00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:15.100
But this was a great panning shot because, you know, Michael says there is no Stanley tree and he's napping.

424
00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:19.460
And then they say, do you think the world is crawling with Phyllis's and she's knitting?

425
00:19:19.460 --> 00:19:21.140
So it was this great visual.

426
00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:22.800
But no, Phyllis can't knit.

427
00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:23.540
Yeah.

428
00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:24.660
No.

429
00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:25.560
No.

430
00:19:25.800 --> 00:19:27.840
That's one of my favorite talking heads, though.

431
00:19:27.940 --> 00:19:28.680
I love that one.

432
00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:29.620
I do, too.

433
00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:30.500
I do, too.

434
00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:33.560
So then Michael is walking around the office.

435
00:19:34.340 --> 00:19:37.580
Dwight can tell something's wrong, but Michael isn't spilling.

436
00:19:37.580 --> 00:19:47.040
And this is my other favorite talking head from this episode, which is Dwight's talking head, where he says, when you're close to someone, you can read them like a book.

437
00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:54.980
And he says, Michael's book is titled, Something Weird is Going On, Colon, What Did Jan Say?

438
00:19:55.480 --> 00:20:00.860
The Michael Scott Story by Michael Scott with Dwight Schrute.

439
00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:04.640
All right, that last part is not in the script,

440
00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:13.100
and I could kind of tell that there was an improv there because whenever Rain improvs at the end of a talking head or the end of a scene,

441
00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:18.700
I feel like you can see him smile just a little bit in the corners of his mouth and his eyes.

442
00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:27.000
So I reached out to Mike Schur, and he told me that he and Rain expanded on the book title on the day, on set.

443
00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:28.480
They kept throwing out ideas.

444
00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:33.280
The original was just supposed to be Something Weird is Going On, Colon, What Did Jan Say?

445
00:20:33.480 --> 00:20:38.940
And Mike threw out the Michael Scott story, and then Rain added with Dwight Schrute.

446
00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:40.080
Yeah, for sure.

447
00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:42.220
I mean, I feel like we all have tells.

448
00:20:42.500 --> 00:20:48.340
And Rain, when he has an improv that I think he's really happy with, has a little bit of a smirk.

449
00:20:48.340 --> 00:20:50.100
He's kind of proud of the moment.

450
00:20:50.320 --> 00:20:52.580
He amuses himself in the moment while saying it.

451
00:20:52.800 --> 00:21:02.020
Now things are really getting heightened over at the Stanford branch because Karen breaks the news that the Scranton branch is closing to Jim, and oh my God, Jim's face.

452
00:21:02.100 --> 00:21:02.920
He's like, what?

453
00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:05.340
You notice he doesn't reach out to Pam.

454
00:21:05.520 --> 00:21:09.460
Pam and Jim never call one another or text one another in this whole day.

455
00:21:09.460 --> 00:21:19.540
It's kind of weird because in Diwali, we see that Pam was texting Jim, and they had that phone call at the end of grief counseling.

456
00:21:20.080 --> 00:21:21.700
But what's going on?

457
00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:23.000
Why no communication?

458
00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:24.900
It makes perfect sense to me.

459
00:21:25.120 --> 00:21:29.800
You know, they're both sort of struggling with where do we go from here?

460
00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:37.960
And I'm sure Pam's first instinct is to reach out to him, but she doesn't feel like she has that kind of access to him anymore.

461
00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:39.440
She rejected him.

462
00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:42.200
So no, it makes perfect sense to me that they don't communicate.

463
00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:47.320
What I thought was weirder, and we're going to get to it, is that Roy finds out from accounting.

464
00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:49.620
So Pam didn't even tell Roy.

465
00:21:49.900 --> 00:21:50.560
That's right.

466
00:21:50.860 --> 00:21:54.120
So now Michael approaches Pam at front reception.

467
00:21:54.340 --> 00:21:55.800
He's acting really strange.

468
00:21:56.000 --> 00:22:02.120
She clearly knows something is up because he was moaning in his office, and Jan visited.

469
00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:04.300
So Pam's like, what's going on, Michael?

470
00:22:05.240 --> 00:22:05.760
Yeah.

471
00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:08.140
I have a fan catch from this moment.

472
00:22:08.480 --> 00:22:09.000
Okay.

473
00:22:09.000 --> 00:22:13.320
At 6 minutes, 21 seconds, Celeste Dimas says,

474
00:22:13.540 --> 00:22:18.800
if you freeze and look closely on that big board that's hanging by accounting,

475
00:22:19.180 --> 00:22:21.700
on Tuesday the 5th, it says,

476
00:22:22.480 --> 00:22:26.380
one of many Emmys, Steve, was robbed.

477
00:22:26.760 --> 00:22:30.400
Oh, that's a great fan catch.

478
00:22:30.540 --> 00:22:32.040
I promise I didn't write it.

479
00:22:32.220 --> 00:22:35.240
We shot this episode about two weeks after the Emmys,

480
00:22:35.240 --> 00:22:40.680
and I guess someone had written up on the board a little congratulations to us,

481
00:22:40.700 --> 00:22:45.280
and we also needed to say that Steve was robbed because he did not win that year for Michael Scott.

482
00:22:45.480 --> 00:22:47.260
He never won for Michael Scott.

483
00:22:47.400 --> 00:22:48.900
Which is ridiculous.

484
00:22:49.380 --> 00:22:49.580
Yeah.

485
00:22:49.580 --> 00:22:56.620
Well, I have a Jenna catch, because since Celeste turned me on to looking at this whiteboard,

486
00:22:56.840 --> 00:22:58.680
I found something else on the whiteboard.

487
00:22:59.000 --> 00:23:04.000
On the top line written under Thursday, written in multiple colors, it says,

488
00:23:04.180 --> 00:23:07.620
in case you haven't noticed, there is a lot of colorful hooey on this board.

489
00:23:09.320 --> 00:23:13.980
Anyway, guys, for the future, I think it could be very fun to freeze on this whiteboard because

490
00:23:13.980 --> 00:23:16.000
they did change what they wrote all the time.

491
00:23:16.000 --> 00:23:16.980
Well, I love that.

492
00:23:17.100 --> 00:23:20.080
I love the little subtle shade towards the television

493
00:23:21.720 --> 00:23:24.040
academy about Steve not getting the Emmy.

494
00:23:24.860 --> 00:23:25.100
Totally.

495
00:23:25.460 --> 00:23:29.440
Coming up next, Michael has a talking head, and then he does something immediately after,

496
00:23:29.640 --> 00:23:32.980
and it's one of these classic Michael moments that I live for.

497
00:23:33.120 --> 00:23:34.540
It always makes me laugh so hard.

498
00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:40.300
Michael says that all he can do is put on a brave face and be our leader.

499
00:23:40.500 --> 00:23:41.860
And then he says

500
00:23:41.860 --> 00:23:44.300
to the whole bullpen, it's over.

501
00:23:44.520 --> 00:23:45.760
We are screwed.

502
00:23:46.240 --> 00:23:46.520
